  "knowledge": {
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETED and verified (0 sorries, axiomCount 0, badge 'original'). A self-contained, axiom-free Lean formalization of the arcsine distribution on [0,1] — CDF F(x) = (2/π)·arcsin(√x). Proves the endpoints (total mass 1), the median at 1/2, monotonicity, the reflection symmetry F(x)+F(1-x)=1, the U-shaped density, and (S2, 2026-06-28) the FTC link F'(x) = f(x) on (0,1) connecting the density to the CDF. S2 also repaired a silent Mathlib-drift breakage (div_le_div_iff rename + stronger field_simp) so the file again compiles exit-0 against the pinned Mathlib v4.26.0. The full probabilistic derivation 'via Brownian motion local times' remains future work (no local-time theory in Mathlib).",
    "builtItems": [
      "Gallery entry src/data/proofs/ballot-problem-oq-02-oq-04 (meta.json + annotations.json); Lean source proofs/Proofs/BallotProblemOQ02OQ04.lean.",
      "S2: hasDerivAt_arcsineCDF / deriv_arcsineCDF (FTC link F'=f on (0,1)); plus build-repair of pre-existing Mathlib-drift errors."
    ],
    "insights": [
      "**The FTC link makes 'density' literal**: arcsineCDF and arcsineDensity began as two unrelated definitions; hasDerivAt_arcsineCDF proves F'(x)=f(x) on (0,1) by the chain rule on arcsin∘√ (Real.hasDerivAt_arcsin ∘ Real.hasDerivAt_sqrt), so the U-shaped f really is the rate of change of the S-shaped F — and density-normalization ∫₀¹f=1 reduces to F(1)−F(0).",
      "**Verified entries silently rot under library drift**: this file passed exit-0 on 2026-06-25 but failed against the same *pinned* Mathlib by 2026-06-28 because div_le_div_iff was renamed and field_simp grew stronger (redundant `ring`s became 'no goals' errors). A 'verified' badge is only as current as the last actual build; single-file `lake env lean` against the pinned oleans is the cheap canonical recheck.",
      "**The arcsin in the name is literal**: the CDF is built directly from Real.arcsin(√x), so every property of the law is a property of a single elementary special function — the formalization needs no measure theory, only real analysis of arcsin and sqrt.",
      "**Reflection symmetry F(x)+F(1−x)=1 is the heart of the matter**: it says the occupation time is distributed symmetrically about 1/2, yet — because the density is U-shaped — symmetry about 1/2 coexists with mass fleeing AWAY from 1/2. The symmetric median and the anti-concentrated density are not in tension; they are the whole surprise of the arcsine law.",
      "**The complementary-angle identity arcsin(√x) + arcsin(√(1−x)) = π/2 is the engine**: it is the analytic shadow of the geometric fact that √x and √(1−x) are sine and cosine of complementary angles, and it is what forces the reflection symmetry. The proof routes through arccos to expose this.",
      "**Honest scoping under a library gap**: Mathlib v4.26.0 has no Brownian motion, no stochastic local time, and no arcsine-distribution object, so the probabilistic 'via local times' derivation cannot be done from primitives. This entry proves exactly the part that IS formalizable — the CDF and density as real-analytic objects — and marks the local-time route as future work rather than axiomatizing it.",
      "**The U-shaped density's minimum at 2/π quantifies the paradox**: the most 'fair' split (half the time positive) is the single least likely outcome, with density bottoming out at 2/π ≈ 0.637, while the density diverges at the extremes 0 and 1."
    ],
